  "href": "utility/utility_preference_relation.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Preference Relation</h1>\n<p>A weak preference relation compares alternatives by the statement that one\nalternative is at least as good as another. From weak preference one derives:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>strict preference, when one alternative is weakly preferred and the reverse\n  weak preference fails;</li>\n<li>indifference, when each alternative is weakly preferred to the other.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For utility theory the natural abstract structure is a total preorder: preference\nis reflexive, transitive, and complete, but it need not be antisymmetric because\ndistinct alternatives can be indifferent.</p>",
